  "api_error_status": null,
  "result": "NRS_484B_493 is done: the gate returned **OK** on its first run (8 witnesses, 18 names, no composition), so 5 of the 6 gate runs are unused.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_493.lean`) applies to a vehicle when all of these hold:\n- **Inside a city:** the `asm.within_incorporated_city` assumption holds.\n- **Notice is posted:** either a `no_standing` or `no_parking` sign whose conditions hold governs a travel region the vehicle occupies, or the vehicle occupies a `no_parking` or `no_stopping` curb zone.\n- **Left-hand side of a one-way roadway:** the vehicle occupies a one-way roadway on a highway, and some road edge to the left of the roadway's direction is strictly nearer its body than every road edge to the right. \"Left\" is the sign of the vehicle's heading dotted with the roadway's direction, times the edge's lateral offset. I wrote it as a product so there's no division.\n\nThe obligation is \"not parked\", using the 0.1 m/s speed tolerance and the 60 s minimum. I added no narrowings: the node left nothing open that needed one.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_493.lean`) use one-way roadway geometry sampled every 5 s. Each one only judges 65–165 s, so the 60 s look-back always has full history. Alongside the five planned scenes I added three branches:\n- `branch_2` (violated): no sign, only a no-parking curb zone.\n- `branch_3` (violated): parked facing against the one-way direction at the left edge, to check the direction sign.\n- `branch_4` (not applicable): a pedestrian instead of a vehicle.\n\nOne shell call was refused: I tried `gate … --help`, which isn't the allowed command. It never ran and didn't use a gate run. `task_result.md` covers this and the full write-up.",
